  "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=8({10}^{x}):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14269080/assets/e9e2aaaedbd98bdd7c27fd3b9a39112f326d35c380d70417528d07aea12a4c4d.png)\n\nNow, let's look at each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false. For $x>0,$ the graph increases without bound as $x$ increases to infinity.\n\n- Statement III is true. $f(1)=8({10}^{1})=8\\cdot 10=80.$ Therefore, the point $(1,80)$ lies on the curve.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and III are true.",
